  "Notes": "Broadband antireflection on glass, 420-680 nm, R below 0.5%\n\nCaveats:\n- Manufacturability is scored with MINT/MAXT (minimum and maximum layer thickness) at a low weight. A sensitivity term (SENS) would score robustness to thickness errors directly, but it needs second derivatives of the merit function and is not offered; MINT/MAXT keep layers depositable and have exact derivatives.\n- L2 norm. With one-sided targets a point that meets its target adds nothing, so once the specification is reachable L2, minimax and L1 find the same design; on a target four layers cannot reach (0.1%) they agree to the third decimal.",
